    "updated_at": "2026-11-08T13:11:19Z",
    "body": "Implementation plan (owner request: \"Intake and complete a camcraft issue\", 2026-11-08)\r\n\r\nScope: #241's reported inability to select the supplied part's planar face/edges and generate facing, trace and contour toolpaths. Base: 8f30beec98d74443a914b872f4e91c620c459dc3. Branch: issue/241-planar-picks. Box selection is a separate enhancement, not part of this correction.\r\n\r\n1. Load the public cutouts.camproj fixture through the real project API; inspect transformed face normals, closed boundary loops and edge chains; exercise operation creation/generation and preserve exact failure evidence.\r\n2. Correct the smallest demonstrated defect in geometry feature topology, app selection resolution or the pick consumer. Retain all safety refusals for invalid/vertical geometry, and do not bypass verification to make a path appear successful. No new language, dependency, datastore, schema or architecture is proposed.\r\n3. Add compact regression geometry reproducing the observed distinguishing preconditions; test the fix against the unmodified base and the candidate. Cover face and edge selection and affected operation kinds through supported command APIs.\r\n4. Use one isolated leaf verifier for baseline reproduction and native focused gates, and a bounded independent reviewer for the final diff. Documentation/decision ledger is a bounded leaf support task. Main implementation stays with Hermes Coder. Each child gets a separate branch/worktree; build cache has one gate owner at a time.\r\n5. Format touched files, run pinning tests then the repository quick gate and affected-crate Clippy with warnings denied. Document unavailable lanes rather than imply they ran. Verify integration against fetched main, then push only the feature branch to the configured owner fork, open a draft PR with Changelog/Fixes and complete evidence, and mark ready after gates hold. No protected-main merge, release, machine output transfer, production access, credential or host changes.\r\n\r\nRisks: the supplied mesh may expose an invalid boundary rather than a UI-only problem; selection repair must not silently fill holes or accept degenerate rings. Open PR #288 changes shell/interaction paths, so avoid those paths unless reproduction proves necessary, then reassess overlap. graphify is not present on the inspected execution paths; current source/tests are the fallback evidence.\r\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
